1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
[narrator] Strange beasts and monsters...

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
vast riches, hidden treasures...

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
evil haunts, uncharted frontiers...

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
the mysterious unknown.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
are called...

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hunters!

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
[theme music plays]

10
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
[Chairman] Huh?

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
One more!

12
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[Gon grunts]

13
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
-[Gon chuckles]
-Hmm?

14
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
-Gotcha! You just used your right hand!
-I did.

15
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,000
[giggles] I did it! Yeah!

16
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
[Gon cheers]

17
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
[snoring gently]

18
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,000
SOLUTION x IS x MAJORITY x RULES

19
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
[narrator] As dawn breaks,

20
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
the airship carrying Gon and his friends
approaches its destination.

21
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The Third Phase of the Hunter Exam
is about to begin.

22
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
-[snoring]
-[PA system tone]

23
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
[Beans] I sincerely apologize
for the long wait.

24
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
The airship will be arriving
at its destination shortly.

25
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[Gon gasps]

26
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[Gon] Is this where the next test
is gonna be held?

27
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
-[man 1] What is this place?
-[man 2] There's nothing here.

28
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,000
[Beans clears throat]

29
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Everyone, this is the site
of the Hunter Exam's Third Phase.

30
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
You'll be competing here
at the top of the Trick Tower.

31
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Did you say Trick Tower?

32
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[Beans] In order to pass this phase,

33
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
you must reach the base
of the tower alive.

34
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
The time limit is 72 hours.

35
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
And with that,
the Exam's Third Phase will now begin.

36
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,000
-Good luck to each and every one of you.
-[crowd murmuring]

37
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
[Lippo snickering]

38
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
[Lippo] So, it's finally my turn, hey?

39
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
[Lippo chewing]

40
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
[Lippo snickering]

41
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
[Beans] All right, everyone. Do your best.

42
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
[grunts]

43
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[Gon] Whoa!

44
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Now what? Are we supposed to climb down?

45
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Well, I hope not. That would be suicide.

46
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
[Number 86 chuckles] Sure, for most guys.

47
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:15,000
[grunts] For an expert rock climber
like me, this is gonna be a piece of cake.

48
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Oh, wow!

49
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Look at how fast he's going!

50
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
[chuckles] By the look of things,

51
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
I'm about to be the first one
to pass the Third Phase.

52
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Huh?

53
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
[distant thudding]

54
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
-[creatures shrieking]
-[Number 86 gasps]

55
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
[screams]
No! Stop! Go away!

56
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Help me!

57
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Uh, so, I guess we can't climb down,
not this way at least.

58
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Yeah.

59
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
-What's up?
-There are fewer people around.

60
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
What?

61
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
[Kurapika] I count 23.

62
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
So nearly half the applicants
have already found an exit.

63
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
No way! When did that happen?

64
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
We're missing something, but what is it?

65
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
There must be hidden doors
up here somewhere

66
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
that lead to the lower floors
of the tower.

67
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Kurapika! Leorio!

68
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
What is it, Gon?

69
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Look at this. We found a trap door.
Check it out!

70
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
[stone scraping]

71
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
[gasping]

72
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
I see, so the only way
that we can reach the lower levels

73
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
-is by turning over these stones.
-Okay, good job!

74
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Now what do you say we head on down?

75
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Okay, but I'm sort of confused.

76
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Why? What is there to be confused about?

77
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
There's one, and another, and another,

78
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
and another one right over there.
There's a lot of them.

79
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
That many?

80
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Five hidden doors
located in the same area.

81
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Sounds a bit suspicious.
No doubt a few of them are traps.

82
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:18,000
From what I can tell, each of these
trap doors can only be used one time.

83
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,000
[Leorio] Seriously?

84
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
[Killua]
We saw somebody fall through one earlier,

85
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
but when we tried to open it,
it wouldn't budge an inch.

86
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Judging by the door's size,

87
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
only one applicant can go through it
at a time.

88
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Which means only one person
can use each door.

89
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
It's beginning to look like
we're all gonna have to split up.

90
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:43,000
We decided that we'll each pick a door,
and see how it goes.

91
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
And no hard feelings
if one of them's a trap.

92
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
How about you guys?
What are you gonna do?

93
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Works for me. Seems like luck
is part of the game or something.

94
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
No objection here. That settles it.

95
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
[Leorio] On the count of three, we all
hop in at exactly the same time, okay?

96
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[Gon] I guess that means
this is goodbye for now, guys.

97
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
We'll meet up at the base of the tower.

98
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Let's do this. One...

99
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
-Two...
-[all] Three.

100
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
[Leorio yelps]

101
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
[all grunt]

102
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
[yelps and groans]

103
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
[groans] Huh?

104
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
[all gasp]

105
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
[Leorio] Wait, what?

106
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[both chuckle]

107
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
-That was certainly a brief farewell.
-No kidding!

108
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
I don't think any of us expected
all those hidden doors

109
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
to lead us all to the same room.

110
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Huh?

111
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
[Gon] Hey, look at this!
"The five who drop into this chamber

112
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,000
must find their way down together
by consensus of the majority.

113
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Wait, five?

114
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Look! They even left us five wrist timers.

115
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
[Killua] With buttons marked X and O.

116
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Do you think it's possible that we won't
be able to leave this room at all

117
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
until someone else drops in
and joins us down here?

118
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[Lippo over speaker] Very good!

119
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Who's there?

120
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
[Lippo] My name is Lippo.
I'm the prison warden here,

121
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
not to mention, your examiner
for the Third Phase of the Exam.

122
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Did he say prison warden?

123
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:24,000
We've gone to the trouble of preparing
multiple routes through the Tower,

124
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
and the one you've chosen
is the path of majority rule.

125
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:33,000
If you want to pass, and I'm sure you do,
co-operation is the essence of success.

126
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,000
One person acting selfishly could derail
the entire group.

127
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:40,000
And of course,
you won't be permitted to start

128
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
until you have five members present.

129
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
That's it, gentlemen. Best of luck!

130
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:50,000
[groans] We seriously can't start
until somebody else shows up?

131
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,000
-So, what now?
-[Kurapika] I guess we just have to wait.

132
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,000
[chair squeaks]

133
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
[whistles]

134
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:13,000
-[prisoner] You wanted to see us, Warden?
-The test begins now.

135
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
So go, take your positions!

136
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
[prisoners] Yes, sir.

137
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,000
[Leorio] Oh, come on!

138
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
We've been sitting here for two hours.

139
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
What if everybody else
already found their way down?

140
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,000
What are we supposed to do, huh?

141
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
We can't be the only ones stuck
at the top, we'll look like total idiots!

142
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,000
[Kurapika]
Calm down, Leorio. Complaining won't help.

143
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Calm down? What if nobody else shows up
before we reach the end of our time limit?

144
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Huh? [groans]

145
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I can't just sit here--

146
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
-Shh! Be quiet.
-Huh?

147
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Do you hear that sound?

148
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
[tapping]

149
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
[stone crumbling]

150
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
[Tonpa groans]

151
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Wow! Good grief!

152
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Mr. Tonpa!

153
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
-Oh, great.
-Look who it is.

154
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Okay.

155
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[rumbling]

156
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
I see.

157
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:33,000
So the door must be programmed to appear
once all five timers are put on.

158
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:38,000
[Gon] "At this door, select O to open,
X not to open."

159
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Using majority rule, already? All right!
At least the answer is obvious.

160
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[Leorio] What?

161
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
'Fess up! Which one of you jokers
hit the X button?

162
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:54,000
[chuckles] That was me. Sorry about that.
I guess I pressed the wrong button.

163
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Stop screwing around, old man!
What, are you blind or something?

164
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
I said it was just an honest mistake.

165
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:05,000
How in the hell do you press
the wrong damn button, huh?

166
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
It doesn't matter. It's okay.
The door's open now.

167
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
[Leorio] It does matter!

168
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
He pressed the wrong button on purpose.
He's trying to sabotage us!

169
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Let's go.
We don't have time for petty bickering.

170
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Yeah, he's right.

171
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Let him keep pressing the wrong button
if he wants to.

172
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
The rest of us will just have to press
the right one.

173
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Fine, I guess.

174
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
[sneers] All right, let's go.

175
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[Leorio grunts angrily]

176
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:37,000
[Leorio] Seriously? I didn't think
we'd get another question so soon.

177
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:42,000
[Gon] "Which way do you want to go?
O for right, X for left."

178
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[Leorio] Right?

179
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Or left?

180
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
[timers beep]

181
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[groans] Hey!
Why would you wanna go right?

182
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
You always go left! What's wrong with you?

183
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
That's true.

184
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:03,000
As research has shown, people who are lost
or find themselves at a crossroads

185
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:06,000
tend to choose to go to the left
much more frequently than the right.

186
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Y'know, I think I've heard that before.

187
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Hold on a second.
The numbers just don't add up!

188
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Which direction did the two of you pick?

189
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
-Right.
-Right.

190
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Ugh. You little monsters...

191
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Going right makes a lot of sense.
The examiner will never see it coming.

192
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
If they've seen the same research
that those two have,

193
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
I bet they made the left path way harder.

194
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,000
[growls] Ugh!

195
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Okay, so we're both simple-minded.
So what?

196
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
[Gon] "We?"

197
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[Leorio gasps] Where the hell are we?

198
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
See that, over there?

199
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:06,000
[prisoner] The applicants are here.
Unlock my handcuffs.

200
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Here we go.

201
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
There, now let's get down to business.

202
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:35,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

203
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:40,000
TONPA

204
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
[Leorio gulps]

205
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
[Lippo over speaker]
Gentlemen, let me explain.

206
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
You've probably already noticed

207
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
that some of the prisoners of Trick Tower
are standing before you.

208
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
They're prisoners?

209
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Lippo] Not just prisoners.

210
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:00,000
The Hunter Exam Committee has also
officially hired them on as examiners.

211
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:05,000
In this phase, you'll be fighting
against all five of them.

212
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
The fights will be one-on-one,
with each person fighting only once.

213
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Use any style you like.
There will be no draws.

214
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:18,000
To be declared the victor,
your opponent must admit defeat.

215
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,000
You can decide which of you will be
the first contender.

216
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
And this is majority rule,

217
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
which means you have to secure three wins
in order to pass.

218
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
The rules are simple.

219
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,000
[sighs] I'm getting real tired of this.

220
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Meh, seems pretty straightforward to me.

221
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Hmm, well, the fights themselves
will be anything but.

222
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,000
For every hour
the prisoners keep you occupied here,

223
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
their sentences will be reduced
by one year.

224
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:52,000
In other words, their goal in this phase
is to literally buy time.

225
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:56,000
I understand. We're on the clock,
and if we don't reach the goal

226
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
of getting out of here in 72 hours,
we fail.

227
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:03,000
So, as you're fighting, remember:
time is of the essence.

228
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Bendot- Robber and murderer
Sentenced to 199 years in prison

229
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Okay, I'm fighting whoever's first.
Now, who's it gonna be?

230
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Now what?
He said to fight however we want,

231
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
so I'm guess that pretty much means
anything goes.

232
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Everybody, be careful.
No telling what they'll try to pull.

233
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Without knowing what's up their sleeves,
there's far too much at stake.

234
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,000
-Given that, I'll--
-[Tonpa] No, I'll go!

235
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Mr. Tonpa?

236
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
I'll be the guinea pig; see if I can
figure out what they're up to.

237
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Consider it an apology for earlier.

238
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Hold on, you're serious?

239
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Sure.

240
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:47,000
You guys don't trust me yet, and I know
I've given you plenty of reasons not to.

241
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,000
If the score ends up being two to two,
who do you want going in there

242
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
to break the tie? 'Cause it ain't me!

243
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
That actually makes sense.

244
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Good, so it's settled then.

245
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Tonpa, so you're...

246
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Hmm.

247
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Well, that was a surprise.
Never thought he'd volunteer.

248
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,000
He didn't really strike me
as the guinea pig type.

249
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Do you guys think he'll be okay?

250
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Now then, let's determine
the method of combat.

251
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
My choice would be a battle to the death.

252
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,000
-[Tonpa gasps]
-A death match?

253
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:50,000
They're gonna fight 'til one of them dies?

254
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:53,000
This is bad.
Don't let him provoke you, Tonpa!

255
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,000
What do you say?

256
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
I accept.

257
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
To the death, then! Let's go!

258
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
-[all gasp]
-Seriously?

259
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
You're a brave man, I'll give you that.

260
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,000
[all grunt]

261
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:34,000
[grunting]

262
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
T-- Tonpa!

263
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Now, begin!

264
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
[roaring]

265
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,000
I give up!

266
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Huh?

267
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
What?

268
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Did he just say that he gives up?

269
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Uh, maybe he meant "give me a sec"?

270
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
[prisoner] What did you just say?

271
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:13,000
I said I admit defeat.
That means you win, right?

272
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:17,000
So, I give up. I lose! [laughs]

273
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Wha-- wha-- what!

274
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:24,000
[prisoner chuckles]

275
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:29,000
All right.
Guess the first round goes to me, then!

276
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:34,000
If we win another two rounds, that's it.
You all fail the exam.

277
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
You can't advance and you can't turn back.

278
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,000
You'll be stuck here
for the next 72 hours,

279
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
until the exam is over.

280
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
And if that happens,

281
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:49,000
our sentences will be reduced
by a grand total of 72 years.

282
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
[cackles]

283
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Oh, man, am I embarrassed!

284
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
He looked a hell of a lot tougher
when I got up close.

285
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Bastard!
I knew we shouldn't have trusted you.

286
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,000
All you're good for is
sabotaging the other applicants!

287
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
You're just a worthless piece of garbage!

288
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:11,000
It took you long enough.
That's what I do every year,

289
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
and I'll keep doing it
for as long as I can.

290
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Wait, say what?

291
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,000
[Tonpa] I don't care about passing
the Hunter Exam.

292
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:22,000
I'm in it for the thrills.
Sorry to disappoint.

293
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
-[Leorio] The thrills?
-[Tonpa] That's right.

294
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
The exam is a proving ground,

295
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:32,000
designed to crush the dreams
of the young and over-confident.

296
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:36,000
And that moment when hope and ambition
give way to absolute despair...

297
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
[chuckles] I get a kick out of that.
The joy I feel is just exquisite.

298
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Especially when I'm the one
actively shattering the newbies' dreams.

299
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
There's nothing like that rush.

300
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,000
I've no desire to be a Hunter.
Doesn't really interest me.

301
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
And I've already had enough fun
for this year.

302
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Besides, I usually stop
at this point anyway.

303
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
-Bastard!
-Leorio, stop!

304
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Why?

305
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:08,000
We're wasting time fighting each other.
That's exactly what they want.

306
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[Leorio grunts]

307
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Yeah, but if their goal was
to kill as much time as possible,

308
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
then the move the old man made
was actually the right one.

309
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[Tonpa] Huh?

310
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:23,000
[Killua] That bald guy looks ex-military,
probably a mercenary.

311
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:27,000
If you'd fought with him,
he'd have started by crushing your larynx.

312
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Pretty hard to give up
if you can't even talk.

313
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Then he'd have tortured you, without
killing you, for as long as he liked.

314
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Yep, I considered that possibility.

315
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
You look sick, old man.

316
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Well, so much for that plan, I guess.

317
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:49,000
I was gonna take my sweet time
torturing the guy until the clock ran out.

318
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:52,000
[Sedokan]
Don't worry. Everything will be fine.

319
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Sedokan -Serial bomber
Sentenced to 149 years in prison

320
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
If we defeat two of the next four,
then victory will be ours.

321
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,000
All right. We need to win three rounds.

322
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,000
It's the only way we'll be able
to advance.

323
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
So, who wants to go next?

324
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Me! I'll give it a try.

325
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
-Are you sure?
-Yeah.

326
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:18,000
[Killua] Well, the next opponent
doesn’t look too strong.

327
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
I wouldn’t let my guard down
if I were you.

328
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
He’s still a hardened criminal.
No telling what he’s capable of.

329
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Yeah, I'll be careful.

330
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:36,000
[narrator] Tonpa’s actions have placed Gon
and his friends at a serious disadvantage.

331
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Their next opponent is Sedokan.

332
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:44,000
As for what exactly he plans to do
in this match, it’s anybody’s guess.

333
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
At the start of the Third Phase
of the Hunter Exam,

334
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,000
there were 40 applicants.

335
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:56,000
And now, with one eliminated,
only 39 remain.

336
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
[theme music plays]

337
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Next time,
"Beware of Prisoners".

338
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
Oh, and watch your back, okay?

339
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[Kurapika]
Be careful when you're out late.
